+## Sales and variance
+
+- `POST /import/sales` takes `{ "csv": "..." }` with the columns
+  `ticket,soldAt,dishId,qty` (`soldAt` is an ISO instant, `qty` a whole
+  number). Each dish sold consumes one portion of its recipe per `qty`, with
+  ledger `ref` `sale:<ticket>` at `soldAt`. Tickets already imported are
+  skipped. Answers `{ "tickets": n, "dishes": n }` (`dishes` is the sum of
+  `qty`). A bad row (`bad_request`) or an item running out (`import_stock`)
+  imports nothing; the message names the row (`row 2` is the first data row).
+- `GET /reports/variance?from=YYYY-MM-DD&to=YYYY-MM-DD` lists, per item,
+  `{ itemId, name, unit, theoretical, actual, difference }`: theoretical use
+  from sales sold in those days (inclusive), actual use from every `consume`
+  movement in those days, and `actual - theoretical`. Items where both are
+  zero are left out.
